WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.300
Template calls are often resolved at instantiation time, not when the generic code is first written.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:13.800
Overload resolution, implicit conversions, and argument-dependent lookup can cause a template to call functions that are not obvious from the template body alone.

3
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.220
This flexibility enables generic libraries, but it can surprise reviewers.

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:25.060
A call that appears to use a standard operation may resolve to a user-defined operation for a particular type.

5
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.600
An unqualified function call may find candidates in namespaces associated with the argument types.

6
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:36.780
An implicit conversion may choose a path that changes cost, exception behavior, or semantics.

7
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.260
Defensive template design limits unnecessary ambiguity.

8
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.720
Qualify names when a specific operation is intended.

9
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.740
Document customization points when extension is intended.

10
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.280
Avoid relying on implicit conversions when they make security-sensitive behavior harder to understand.

11
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:58.760
Review should consider what code may actually run for important instantiations.

12
00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:05.580
This is especially important for comparison, hashing, formatting, allocation, serialization, cleanup, and policy decisions.

13
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:11.200
The operation selected for one type may not preserve the assumptions tested with another type.

14
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.040
The goal is not to disable extensibility.

15
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.940
The goal is to make extensibility deliberate.

16
00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:24.160
Generic APIs should make clear which operations can be customized and which operations are fixed by the library.

17
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:31.240
When behavior must be fixed, use qualified calls or helper functions that enforce the intended operation.

18
00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:38.860
When behavior is intentionally customizable, name that extension point and test at least one custom implementation.
